                    "value": "PRIMARY: stratified 80/20 patient holdout; development-only cross-validation selects regularization. Preprocessing is fitted within each training fold.\n\nSECONDARY: 2010–2013 development, 2014–2015 validation, 2016–2017 temporal test. Model eligibility remains 2010–2017 for the existing source era.\n\nSOURCES: Brain, Breast, Prostate and Skin coursework extracts have no usable stage. Liver uses explicit source summary stage. Grade is not a stage proxy.\n\nLIMITS: revised internal evaluation of the supplied sampled dataset. Prior results were inspected. No independent confirmatory validation, clinical risk estimate, treatment-effect claim, or individual recommendation is established.\n\nDESIGN: ratios and discrimination measures are never averaged across cancer types. Select a cancer to inspect metrics; report pages keep descriptive and model populations separate.",
